1
00:00:07,653 --> 00:00:10,974
A phone has a cracked screen.
Is it still the same phone?

2
00:00:11,785 --> 00:00:16,542
Under the logic of substance, the
answer is hidden in the thing itself.

3
00:00:16,622 --> 00:00:18,743
A thing is what its essence makes it.

4
00:00:18,823 --> 00:00:22,361
It stays the same for as
long as the essence remains.

5
00:00:23,165 --> 00:00:26,074
The logic of dependency
moves the question.

6
00:00:26,154 --> 00:00:29,498
Identity is not what a thing is in itself.

7
00:00:29,578 --> 00:00:33,900
It is how the thing is reliably
picked out. So "is it the same?"

8
00:00:33,980 --> 00:00:39,624
becomes: the same by which criteria? For
which purpose? Within which framework?

9
00:00:40,438 --> 00:00:44,190
The phone with the cracked screen is
the same phone for the repair shop,

10
00:00:44,270 --> 00:00:45,549
and for the insurer.

11
00:00:45,628 --> 00:00:50,752
A ship whose every plank has been
replaced is the same ship on the register.

12
00:00:50,832 --> 00:00:54,584
For the museum that kept the
old planks, perhaps it is not.

13
00:00:54,664 --> 00:00:57,002
The child in an old photograph is you.

14
00:00:57,082 --> 00:00:59,856
You for your family, for
your birth certificate,

15
00:00:59,936 --> 00:01:03,352
and for the story that runs
from that afternoon to this one.

16
00:01:04,165 --> 00:01:06,829
Each answer is correct
within its framework.

17
00:01:06,909 --> 00:01:10,611
None of them is found in the
thing, apart from the framework.

18
00:01:11,430 --> 00:01:13,837
This does not make identity arbitrary.

19
00:01:13,917 --> 00:01:17,166
Criteria can be applied
correctly or wrongly.

20
00:01:17,246 --> 00:01:19,829
They are tested against
further experience.

21
00:01:19,909 --> 00:01:21,785
A forged passport fails.

22
00:01:21,865 --> 00:01:25,549
A mistaken face in a crowd
is corrected when it turns.

23
00:01:25,629 --> 00:01:30,712
What has gone is only one further claim:
that beneath the criteria lies a sameness

24
00:01:30,792 --> 00:01:34,901
from the thing's own side, which
the criteria merely detect.

25
00:01:35,722 --> 00:01:41,240
Identity seemed the most undeniable
thing there was. This is this. I am me.

26
00:01:41,320 --> 00:01:44,447
Seen through dependency,
it is not less real.

27
00:01:44,527 --> 00:01:47,042
Its reality is of a different kind.

28
00:01:47,122 --> 00:01:50,208
It is the reality of a
designation that works:

29
00:01:50,288 --> 00:01:54,370
a name, given within a
framework, that does its job.

30
00:01:55,190 --> 00:01:58,099
The same shift changes
the word "conventional".

31
00:01:58,179 --> 00:02:01,333
The logic of substance
hears it as a demotion.

32
00:02:01,413 --> 00:02:04,893
What is conventional is
agreed on, perhaps arbitrary,

33
00:02:04,973 --> 00:02:06,768
certainly less than real.

34
00:02:06,848 --> 00:02:10,020
The real would be there
whether anyone agreed or not.

35
00:02:10,856 --> 00:02:15,789
For the logic of dependency, conventional
truth is the only kind of validity there

36
00:02:15,869 --> 00:02:19,580
is. And it is fully
valid. It has standards.

37
00:02:19,660 --> 00:02:25,205
Tsongkhapa gives three criteria, to sort
sound conventions from mistaken ones.

38
00:02:25,285 --> 00:02:28,738
A valid convention is known
to ordinary cognition.

39
00:02:28,818 --> 00:02:32,393
It is not overturned by
further ordinary cognition.

40
00:02:32,473 --> 00:02:36,052
And it is not contradicted
by analysis of the ultimate.

41
00:02:36,900 --> 00:02:39,143
Think of a rope seen as a snake.

42
00:02:39,223 --> 00:02:43,464
The snake fails the second test:
a closer look overturns it.

43
00:02:43,544 --> 00:02:47,336
The rope taken as existing
in itself fails the third.

44
00:02:47,416 --> 00:02:50,543
The rope as named and
used passes all three.

45
00:02:50,623 --> 00:02:53,328
Convention is not the opposite of truth.

46
00:02:53,408 --> 00:02:57,599
It is where truth, in
every usable sense, lives.

47
00:02:58,405 --> 00:03:01,287
What changes is the
status of the undeniable.

48
00:03:01,367 --> 00:03:04,765
That this table is simply
here. That I am simply me.

49
00:03:04,845 --> 00:03:06,572
That time simply flows.

50
00:03:06,652 --> 00:03:10,730
Each is a designation so
reliable, and so habitual,

51
00:03:10,810 --> 00:03:14,140
that its being a designation
has become invisible.

52
00:03:14,220 --> 00:03:17,238
Seeing this costs none of its reliability.

53
00:03:17,318 --> 00:03:22,419
It loses only its claim to stand outside
the framework that makes it reliable.

54
00:03:23,238 --> 00:03:27,859
There is no second, deeper truth
for convention to fall short of.

55
00:03:27,939 --> 00:03:30,604
Ultimate truth is not a higher world.

56
00:03:30,684 --> 00:03:32,710
It is the emptiness of this one.

57
00:03:32,790 --> 00:03:37,357
The conventional table, the conventional
self and the conventional hour are not

58
00:03:37,437 --> 00:03:39,345
found from their own side.

59
00:03:40,149 --> 00:03:42,356
One appearance, seen two ways.

